{
  "area": "bonaire",
  "method": "Bonaire and Klein Bonaire: the whole Bonaire National Marine Park, west coast from Boka Bartol to Willemstoren Lighthouse, the Lac Bay east-coast sites and the Klein Bonaire ring. Official list: STINAPA's current Bonaire National Marine Park dive-site map (sites 01-61 on Bonaire, A-Z on Klein Bonaire, linked from stinapabonaire.org/bonaire-national-marine-park as 'Download our Dive Site Map'), counted as one list; the same STINAPA page and its rules page are the authority for closures. Operator lists, one each: Buddy Dive Resort's 2025-26 brochure site table (1-63 plus Klein Bonaire), Beyond the Corals' dive-site page (same numbering), Dive Friends Bonaire's staff-picks site list, and VIP Diving's top-five site list; Buddy Dive's east-coast page is Buddy Dive again and adds no list. The Tourism Corporation Bonaire site directory (bonaireisland.com, 20 entries) counts as one tourism-board list; its single 'Andrea 1 & 2' entry is credited to both Andreas. Captain Don's Habitat, Bruce Bowker's Carib Inn, Wannadive, Harbour Village and Toucan Diving were read but publish no site list (only a house reef or 'over 50 moored sites'), Great Adventures' site renders no text and Bonaire Dive & Adventure's domain is parked, so none of them is counted; bonaire.com, infobonaire.com, divers-guide, DivePlannerPro and PADI pages were read for leads only. A site is counted when it is named, recreationally divable and on at least two of these lists; names follow the STINAPA map with the operators' alternative names as aliases (C 'Jerry's Reef' is the operators' 'Jerry's Sponges'). Excluded: the six Washington Slagbaai National Park sites (01-06), because STINAPA states the park remains closed for diving; Town Pier, which the map marks closed under the ISPS code; Twixt and Vallerie's Hill, on the STINAPA map only; and Yellow Submarine and Turtle City, each on one operator list only. No list gives coordinates, so no positions are recorded. Counted 2026-10-14.",
